  "narrative": "The feature_063 evidence supports a broader association but does not yet fully settle whether it is dataset-wide or context-dependent. H67 is the cleanest direct non-residual stratum: feature_063=1 versus 0 among feature_002=1/feature_037=0/feature_010=0. Because the hypothesis direction is negative, the signed estimate +0.390 corresponds to a raw outcome_001 difference of about -0.390 composite dependency-score units, with the signed interval +0.202 to +0.578 entirely above the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction. The cells are valid but small, especially 36 exposed observations, so I accept the discovery evidence but keep the investigation active and request independent validation. H66 tests the overall marginal association: signed +0.227, raw about -0.227, signed interval +0.131 to +0.323. The point is above threshold and the interval excludes zero, but the lower bound is below 0.15, so overall meaningfulness remains unresolved. H75 is in the right direction, raw about -0.227, but its signed lower bound is only +0.072, so the data cannot rule out subthreshold magnitude. H76 has a positive signed point estimate, but its interval spans negative signed values and large positive values, meaning the raw effect is not stabilized in the claimed direction. Therefore H75 and H76 remain unresolved and active. The interaction claims H77-H79 test attenuation of feature_063 when feature_037, feature_002, or feature_010 is present. H77 and H79 have near-zero point estimates with intervals that do not support a meaningful attenuation effect, so they are rejected. H78 has a negative signed estimate, which is opposite the hypothesized attenuation direction and would imply a somewhat stronger raw negative feature_063 effect when feature_002=1 in the tested complement; the upper bound does not support claimed positive attenuation, so H78 is rejected. The residual-stratum low-frequency flag screens H71-H74 are all near zero or opposite to the claimed negative direction and are rejected. H82, a broad nominal categorical screen of feature_059 level_001 versus level_003, has a small point estimate and interval entirely below the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction, so it is rejected. These conclusions remain descriptive associations in the supplied dataset and should not be interpreted as causal, biological, mechanistic, or generalizable findings.",
  "research_notes": "Central accepted dataset associations: feature_037=1 lowers outcome_001; feature_010=1 raises outcome_001; feature_002=1 raises outcome_001. feature_063=1 lowers outcome_001 in the validated residual stratum feature_002=0/feature_037=0/feature_010=0. New direct stratum H67, feature_002=1/feature_037=0/feature_010=0, is accepted on discovery but kept active and independently validated because the exposed cell is small. H66 overall feature_063 is suggestive but unresolved because signed lower bound 0.131 is below threshold. H75 and H76 are uncertain direct strata. Attenuation interactions H77-H79 are rejected, so current evidence favors either a broadly persistent or context-variable feature_063 association rather than clear attenuation. Residual low-frequency flags feature_022, feature_028, feature_064, and feature_013 are null in this dataset, as is the feature_059 level_001 versus level_003 screen. Next analyses should complete broad feature_063 strata H68-H70, finish residual flags H80-H81, and run categorical screens H83-H86. Interpret any categorical result cautiously because levels are nominal and screens are multiplicity-prone. Reassess H67 immediately when validation arrives. Do not claim causality or generalizability.",
